  "provider_query": "Which organization does the CVE program identify as the source of CVE records used by NVD",
  "answer": "The CVE Program identifies the **CVE List** as the source of the CVE records that NVD uses. That list was launched by **The MITRE Corporation** and is maintained under the CVE Program (operated by MITRE as a DHS/CISA-sponsored FFRDC effort).\n\nConcise sourcing:\n\n1. **CVE Program (cve.org, Related Efforts)** — CVE and NVD are separate. The CVE List was launched by The MITRE Corporation in 1999; NVD was launched by NIST in 2005. “The CVE List feeds NVD,” which builds on CVE Records.  \n   https://www.cve.org/about/relatedefforts\n\n2. **CVE Program FAQs** — Same relationship: the CVE List (MITRE, 1999) feeds NVD (NIST, 2005), which adds enrichment such as fix information, severity scores, and impact ratings. CVE Records are used by products and services including NVD.  \n   https://www.cve.org/ResourcesSupport/FAQs\n\n3. **NVD General FAQs (NIST)** — The CVE Program is maintained by the MITRE Corporation and sponsored by DHS/CISA. NVD augments the CVE List and stays synchronized with it; updates to the CVE List appear in NVD. NVD ingests the CVE List about hourly.  \n   https://nvd.nist.gov/general/FAQ-Sections/General-FAQs\n\n4. **NVD CVE FAQs** — After a CNA or the CVE Assignment Team publishes a record to the Official CVE List, NVD enriches it (references, CVSS, CWE, CPE, and related data).  \n   https://nvd.nist.gov/general/FAQ-Sections/CVE-FAQs\n\n5. **NVD “CVEs and the NVD Process”** — The CVE Program is maintained by MITRE and sponsored by DHS/CISA. CVE IDs are assigned by MITRE and by CVE Numbering Authorities (CNAs). Records published to the CVE List typically appear in NVD within about an hour.  \n   https://nvd.nist.gov/general/cve-process\n\n6. **CVE Program history (cve.org)** — NIST’s NVD is described as synchronized with and based upon the CVE List.  \n   https://www.cve.org/about/history\n\n7. **Official CVE List (CVEProject/cvelistV5)** — The GitHub repository is the official CVE List: a catalog of CVE Records identified by or reported to the CVE Program, in CVE JSON 5 format.  \n   https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5\n\n8. **Who publishes the records** — Individual CVE Records are created and published by CNAs (and CNA-LRs) partnered with the CVE Program; MITRE also acts as CNA of Last Resort and runs secretariat functions. NVD does not originate the CVE IDs or the base CVE List content.  \n   https://www.cve.org/ResourcesSupport/FAQs\n\n**Bottom line:** The organization the CVE Program points to as the origin of the list NVD consumes is **The MITRE Corporation** (CVE Program / CVE List). NVD (NIST) is a downstream consumer and enrichment layer, not the source of the CVE records.",
